upx_packed_pe_i386.exe -- the UPX-packed win32/pe fixture for `kuna unpack` /
`kuna_analysis::upx::pe`.

What it is
  A 32-bit MSVC Windows GUI crackme packed with UPX 1.25. 22,016 bytes packed;
  49,152 bytes unpacked. Unlike the ELF witness next to it, its UPX! PackHeader
  is NOT in the tail: it sits in the header padding at 0x3e0, immediately before
  the compressed block, and reads version=12, format=9 (win32/pe), method=2
  (NRV2B_LE32), level=4, filter=0x26 (cto32_e8e9). One compressed block:
  0x454e bytes in, 0xc6a0 out.

  It exercises every part of the PE arm at once -- the header-padding PackHeader,
  the single-block layout, the trailer that carries the original PE header and
  section table, the import rebuild (4 DLLs, 79 imports by name), and the
  resource rebuild (3 leaves, two of which UPX moved out of the image).

  It also carries one thing a stock `upx -o` output does not: the section table
  was renamed to .text/.data/.rsrc/.reloc and a fourth section was appended with
  a decoy import directory (Kernel32.dll!Beep) that the PE data directory points
  at, so the real loader import table has to be found by agreement with the
  trailer rather than read out of the directory. That is why it is the fixture.

Why it is vendored rather than built
  `upx` is not a build dependency of this repo and is not installed on CI, so a
  packed fixture cannot be produced at build time -- and no packer targeting
  win32/pe runs on the Linux CI image at all.

Where it came from
  The RE-friction loop's round-6 witness: challenge 5ab77f5433c5d40ad448c1cd in
  the kuna-re-dataset crackme corpus ("end_of_the_world by ultrasound",
  https://crackmes.one/crackme/5ab77f5433c5d40ad448c1cd), `bin/EndOfWorld.zip.__x/
  EndOfWorld.exe`, byte-identical. That is the binary on which a tester found
  `kuna unpack` exiting 1 with "no UPX PackHeader found" and filed
  docs/re-needs/unpack-proceed-without-upx.md.

  sha256(packed)   see `sha256sum upx_packed_pe_i386.exe`
  It is a third-party crackme, included unmodified as test data only.
